00:01:57,210 --> 00:01:59,240
 The first intro to robots--

40
00:01:59,240 --> 00:02:01,320
 does anyone know that robots--

41
00:02:01,320 --> 00:02:05,930
 the word robots started from 1920, right?

42
00:02:05,930 --> 00:02:08,570
 Weeks here.

43
00:02:08,570 --> 00:02:12,330
 So the word robot comes from the Czech word robota, which

44
00:02:12,330 --> 00:02:14,740
 means forced labor and servitude.

45
00:02:14,740 --> 00:02:18,370
 It started as a playwright, like a theater play.

46
00:02:18,370 --> 00:02:20,950
 And we don't know the word Czech Republic.

47
00:02:20,950 --> 00:02:24,230
 It's next to Germany, Austria, and Poland.

48
00:02:24,230 --> 00:02:29,950
 And Poland as well, because you're a neighbor.

49
00:02:29,950 --> 00:02:34,610
 And the idea is to showcase how having something like robots

50
00:02:34,610 --> 00:02:39,800
 can do human labor at scale very efficiently.

51
00:02:39,800 --> 00:02:41,700
 It spread really quickly through Europe

52
00:02:41,700 --> 00:02:42,800
 when that day came up.

53
00:02:42,800 --> 00:02:45,720
 It's funny, because the critics of the theater,

54
00:02:45,720 --> 00:02:47,790
 they were pretty harsh on the theater play,

55
00:02:47,790 --> 00:02:49,230
 but people really loved this.

56
00:02:49,230 --> 00:02:51,560
 Loved it in the sense they were very interested

57
00:02:51,560 --> 00:02:53,040
 about the concept.

58
00:02:53,040 --> 00:02:55,270
 And a lot of it was driven by fear,

59
00:02:55,270 --> 00:02:58,200
 because it shows that humans can be replaced by machines.

60
00:02:58,200 --> 00:03:03,430
 So all this fear about AI replacing us started from 1920.

61
00:03:03,430 --> 00:03:06,920
 Fear would never go away.

62
00:03:06,920 --> 00:03:09,560
 OK, after that, the actual real robot

63
00:03:09,560 --> 00:03:12,720
 that started autonomous robot was 1948.

64
00:03:12,720 --> 00:03:14,760
 This LC, the torch voice.

65
00:03:14,760 --> 00:03:16,800
 And it had a very simple task.

66
00:03:16,800 --> 00:03:20,000
 All it did was it can move around, and all it needs--

67
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:23,700
 all it does is it can see light and goes towards it.

68
00:03:23,700 --> 00:03:27,120
 So if you're in a spot in a cave and you have this torch voice,

69
00:03:27,120 --> 00:03:29,120
 it can guide you maybe through the light at the end

70
00:03:29,120 --> 00:03:31,740
 of the tunnel, as they say.

71
00:03:31,740 --> 00:03:33,260
 And it had some nice functionality.

72
00:03:33,260 --> 00:03:37,020
 It wasn't very sophisticated, because it was the first one.

73
00:03:37,020 --> 00:03:39,540
 And it can avoid obstacles.

74
00:03:39,540 --> 00:03:43,200
 The good thing is like Roomba, the vacuum in your home.

75
00:03:43,200 --> 00:03:49,980
 It can go back and recharge whenever it needs batteries.

76
00:03:49,980 --> 00:03:54,570
 OK, so personal assistants are very, very important.

